<speak>Thank you, Marcus. I am comfortable; I have the telephone on its stand rather than holding it. That was another small improvement my niece suggested. I used to wedge it between my shoulder and my ear while looking through papers, and then wonder why my neck felt stiff. These days I try to set things up properly before the call. It sounds rather obvious when I say it aloud, but it took me a long time to change the habit.</speak>